# CR 400.7: De-evolve's threshold trigger goes on the stack at Bot2's upkeep; Bot2 returns the enchanted Memnite to its
# owner's hand in response, and De-evolve goes to the graveyard (CR 704.5m). The trigger still resolves - eight cards in
# Bot1's graveyard - but "exile enchanted creature" names the Memnite that left: the card in Bot1's hand is a new object
# and is not exiled. (Before the core skipped stale objects in every move, this exiled a second Memnite and left the one
# in hand as well.)
# De-evolve {1}{B}: Enchantment — Aura
#   Enchant creature
#   Enchanted creature gets -4/-0, can't block, and is a Salamander. (It loses all other creature types.)
#   Threshold — At the beginning of each upkeep, if there are seven or more cards in your graveyard, exile enchanted creature.

[Bot1 Deck]
De-evolve
Thought Scour
Thought Scour
Memnite
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Unsummon
Island x20

[Opening]
Chooser: Bot1

[Actions]
Bot1.DrawFirst
Bot1.Keep
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Pass
